{
  "why": [
    "A declared status may be a single value or a LIST of acceptable ones.",
    "Cases that read a live source declare [\"Passed\",\"Blocked\"]: the invariant held, or the source was unreachable and nothing was measured.",
    "What no list ever contains is Failed. An unreachable node must never be reported as an insolvent protocol.",
    "Case 2 is always Blocked: it carries an assertion that cannot be observed at all.",
    "No case is declared Failed. Nothing here is currently failing, and manufacturing a failure to have one would be dishonest.",
    "PerpDEX cases (43-163) are deterministic on anvil. They declare [\"Passed\",\"Blocked\"] only because a run without the local chain must grade Blocked, never Failed; with the chain up, every one of them is expected to Pass.",
    "DB (164-189) and mini-api (190-229) cases are deterministic on anvil with the indexer and REST service running; they declare [\"Passed\",\"Blocked\"] for the same reason as PerpDEX -- a run without the local chain or service must grade Blocked, never Failed.",
    "Bot risk-gate cases (230-237) and the retry/no-secret cases (256, 260) are pure functions with no external source, so they declare a single \"Passed\"; the bot cases that drive PerpDEX declare [\"Passed\",\"Blocked\"] like every other anvil tier.",
    "The expanded GMX contract (265-281) and API (282-301) cases read the live Arbitrum RPC and GMX public endpoints, so they declare [\"Passed\",\"Blocked\"] -- an unreachable node or venue is Blocked, never Failed."
  ],
